>2) I've heard that #dipping a weapon into a fountain could be beneficial.
>   Now all my weapons are thoroughly rusted and I never got anything but
>   a +4 on Powerpoints (for a Samurai). Was I misinformed?

There are three times when you might want to dip something into a
fountain:

1)  It's cursed.  Dipping it will sometimes uncurse it.
2)  It's a longsword, and you're lawful.  You might get a powerful
artifact.
3)  It's a potion, scroll, or spellbook that you want to dilute or
blank out.

>3) I ate a water nymph corpse and teleported at random times to random places.
>   When I tried to buy something in a shop, I teleported out accidentaly and
>   had the shopkeeper and kops after me. Is there a way to pay your debt
>   afterwards and make the shopkeeper peaceful again?

If you've only recently robbed the shop, you can p)ay the shopkeeper.
Otherwise, unless you can defeat or outrun him, you're out of luck.

Eating nymph corpses is not reccomended unless you have a means of
teleport control.

>4) How does one train a pet? Or is it just growing stronger with time and
>   doesn't learn any new tricks? I'd like to be able to send my dog somewhere.

Throwing tripe at a pet (if it's a dog or cat, or polymorphed into
one) right after it does something may train it to do it again.  The
only things that I know pets can be trained to do are rob shops and
walk on cursed items.


